description:
Line 175-220: `Fragment::from_bytes` extracts `rule_id` from wire data but never validates it:
```rust
let rule_id = data[0];
// ... no call to check_rule(rule_id)?
```

In contrast, `Fragment::write_to` (line 134), `Ack::write_to` (line 243), and `Control::write_to` (line 380) all call `check_rule()`.

This creates an asymmetry: you can parse a fragment with rule_id >= 128, but then fail when trying to re-serialize it.

The `FragmentReceiver::receive` method does call `check_rule` (line 830), but direct callers of `Fragment::from_bytes` bypass this check.

Suggested fix: Add `check_rule(rule_id)?` after extracting rule_id in `from_bytes`:
```rust
let rule_id = data[0];
check_rule(rule_id)?;
```
